From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 07:57:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wintrust: close the trust data the caller just handed us, not
 the one verify saw.

WinVerifyTrust with WTD_STATEACTION_CLOSE takes its own WINTRUST_DATA, and the
provider data it looks the state up from still points at the structure the
earlier WTD_STATEACTION_VERIFY call was given. The close path then walks that
old pointer: SoftpubCleanup, among other things, closes the file it opened and
stores INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE back into pWintrustData->pFile->hFile. A caller is
entitled to have freed or reused that structure once verify returned, so the
write lands in whatever occupies the memory now.

Measured: Office's Click-to-Run installer faults exactly there.

  wine: Unhandled page fault on write access to 00006FFFF9BDCFC0
  wine:   00006FFFF92EE235  L"wintrust.dll" +0xe235
  wine:   00006FFFF9BE499E  L"crypt32.dll"  +0x4499e

which disassembles to the movq of INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE into pFile->hFile inside
SoftpubCleanup. The thread dies holding the install's lock and setup.exe hangs
behind it for as long as it is left running. With the close using the structure
it was passed the same install runs to completion with no fault at all.

The structure passed to close is the one the caller is vouching for at that
moment, so point the provider data at it before cleanup runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d39d43347c9b5d26b0a2ef57cc79ea6bd1ddc075)

diff --git a/dlls/wintrust/wintrust_main.c b/dlls/wintrust/wintrust_main.c
index a9b1587e5be..44a61277967 100644
--- a/dlls/wintrust/wintrust_main.c
+++ b/dlls/wintrust/wintrust_main.c
@@ -307,6 +307,20 @@ static LONG WINTRUST_DefaultClose(HWND hwnd, GUID *actionID,
 
     if (provData)
     {
+        /* Cleanup reaches back through pWintrustData -- SoftpubCleanup resets
+         * the file handle it opened, among other things -- and that pointer is
+         * still the WINTRUST_DATA the verify call was given.  A caller that
+         * verifies and then closes is free to have reused or freed that
+         * structure in between, and following the stale pointer writes into
+         * whatever now occupies the memory.  Measured: Office's Click-to-Run
+         * installer faults there, in SoftpubCleanup's
+         * pFile->hFile = INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, and the install deadlocks
+         * behind the dead thread.
+         *
+         * The structure passed to close is the one the caller is vouching for,
+         * so point at that. */
+        provData->pWintrustData = data;
+
         if (provData->psPfns->pfnCleanupPolicy)
             err = provData->psPfns->pfnCleanupPolicy(provData);
 
